@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# RC5 pipeline repair
+
+RC4 introduced a reserved WGSL identifier (`coherent`) in the BreakerLip
+validity guard, in addition to adding weather calls to its vertex stage. The
+previous material test never installed this guard. The full runtime inventory
+reproduced the reserved-keyword compiler error. RC5 restores the exact RC3
+guard and removes the RC4 vertex-stage weather calls. Spray's restored path,
+asset caching, incremental evidence uploads and other RC4 fixes are retained.
+
+Optional BreakerLip failure removes only its transparent mesh. Crest detection,
+surface rollers and the core ocean continue. The real invalid-WGSL regression
+test verifies its error cannot poison the enclosing startup validation scope.
+Compile errors are non-retryable; core failures stop after one attempt. Network
+and device-loss recovery retain the cellular retry policy. Detailed compiler
+messages are recorded. Degraded optional effects invalidate the full-effects
+FPS gate rather than silently producing an easier performance pass.
+
+The old six-material module-only check has been replaced with a runtime graph
+inventory: 79 render/compute descriptors and 78 unique shader modules, including
+the native guard, forecast FFT, weather cache, sky, lips, spray, rain and post.
+Dawn's strict WGSL validation passes all modules and rejects the exact RC4 bug.
+Inventory generation is explicitly not compilation or GPU execution.
+
+Apple WebKit CI replays every module, binding layout, entry point and pipeline.
+It fails for compilation errors, missing adapters, timeouts or incomplete results.
+Packaging requires the matching manifest SHA-256 and successful full compiler
+report. No report means no release. The CI result is separate from physical
+iPhone screenshots and the unchanged 120-second cadence test.
+
+Automated checks: seven interaction checks (scene look, sun drag, timeline,
+pinch/reset, water sheet, Back to now, Watch pause); startup retry classification;
+optional-effect isolation using a real invalid WebGPU shader; strict WGSL;
+existing build, production and visual/source budget checks. No new phone FPS or
+rendered-pixel claim is made. Current Apple CI result must be attached before
+this candidate can be deployed.
